          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+electrodynamics"} quantum electrodynamics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            the
            %em Schwinger limit
            is a maximal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\;\approx\;
                  \\frac{
                  m^2 c^3
                  }{
                  e \hbar
                  }
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background field
            beyond which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+polarization"} vacuum polarization
            caused by pair creation
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positrons"} positrons
            or
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antiparticle"} anti
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+decay"} vacuum decay
          %p
            From the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"}> holographic QCD
            ) the Schwinger limit corresponds to the limiting field strength in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI-action"} DBI-action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+Schwinger+effect"}> holographic Schwinger effect
            ”).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
            and its resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+limit"} Schwinger limit
            are securely prediuted by established
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            yet. However, recent experiments are getting very close and upcoming experiments might see the effect.
          %h2#details Details
          %p From the rate
          #eq:SchwingerEffectAtGeneralFieldStrengthForWeakCoupling.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mi ℬ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %msup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mi coth
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mi n
                    %mi π
                    %mo )
                  %mi exp
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi m
                          %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mi ℰ
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma
                  \\;=\;
                  \\frac
                  {
                  e^2 \mathcal{E} \mathcal{B}
                  }{
                  8 \pi^2
                  }
                  \\underoverset
                  {n = 1}
                  {\infty}
                  {\sum}
                  \\frac{1}{n}
                  \\coth
                  \\left(
                  \\frac{\mathcal{B}}{\mathcal{E}} n \pi
                  \\right)
                  \\exp
                  \\left(
                  \-
                  \\frac{
                  m^2 \pi n
                  }{
                  e \mathcal{E}
                  }
                  \\right)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "Schwinger+effect#eq:SchwingerEffectAtGeneralFieldStrengthForWeakCoupling"}> here
            ) of particle pair creation via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
            one deduces a critical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{crit}
            which sets the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
            beyond which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+polarization"} vacuum polarization
            due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
            counteracts the ambient electric field and/or leads to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+decay"} vacuum decay
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            (
            %a{:href => "Schwinger+effect#eq:LorentzInvariantFieldStrenghts"}> here
            ) this
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+limit"} Schwinger limit
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            is:
          #eq:CriticalFieldStrengthLorentzInvariant.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\frac{
                  m^2 c^3
                  }{
                  e \hbar
                  }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dunne04"}> Dunne 04, (1.3)
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Martin07"} Martin 07, (40)
          %p Here
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particles"} charged particles
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particles"} charged particles
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/speed+of+light"} speed of light
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
          %p
            This is such that the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+force"} Lorentz force
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi crit
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi e
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_{crit}
                  \\; \coloneqq \;
                  e
                  \\,
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
          %p
            acting over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Compton+wavelength"} Compton wavelength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi Comp
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{Comp} \;\coloneqq\; \frac{\hbar }{m c}
            equals the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rest+energy"} rest energy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m c^2
            of the given
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particle"} charged particle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi crit
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi Comp
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi m
                          %msup
                            %mi c
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mi crit
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %msup
                                %mi c
                                %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %msub
                                %mi λ
                                %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \&amp;
                  F_{crit} \lambda_{Comp}
                  \\; = \;
                  m c^2
                  \\\
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  \\;\;\;
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\; = \;
                  \\frac{
                  m c^2
                  }{
                  e \lambda_{Comp}
                  }
                  \\end{aligned}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_dbilimit Relation to DBI-limit
          %p
            Expressing
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CriticalFieldStrengthLorentzInvariant"} (2)
            in terms of the corresponding critical value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
